          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.517,
            0.563,
            0.816,
            0.586
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "④Sarcomeres become shorter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.594,
            0.909,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12.The sheep \"Dolly\" was cloned by introducing a nucleus from the mammary gland of a mature female sheep into an enucleated egg cell. Dolly, therefore, has:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.689,
            0.957,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "index": 26,
              "bbox": [
                0.165,
                0.69,
                0.957,
                0.744
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "①A nuclear genome from one cellular source and an organellar genome from another source;"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "index": 27,
              "bbox": [
                0.164,
                0.754,
                0.844,
                0.783
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "②Nuclear and mitochondrial genomes from the same cellular source;"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "index": 28,
              "bbox": [
                0.165,
                0.788,
                0.38,
                0.811
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "③A haploid genome;"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "index": 29,
              "bbox": [
                0.164,
                0.82,
                0.955,
                0.877
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "④More potential to transmit genetic variation to her offspring than animals produced as a result of sexual reproduction."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "sub_type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 30,
          "bbox": [
            0.877,
            0.934,
            0.969,
            0.956
          ],
          "content": [
